From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Pitoiset <samuel.pitoiset@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:03:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] radv/rt: fix overwriting stack size on partial cache hits

On a partial cache hit, the binaries and the RT stack size are
restored. But in some cases (eg. for libraries), the NIR needs to be
recompiled and it was overwriting the previous stack size.

This caused some (very rare) random VM faults with
dEQP-VK.ray_tracing_pipeline.pipeline_library.configurations.rgen_miss_in_library.*
because scratch was supposed to be enabled but it wasn't due to the
stack size being 0.

This has been very hard to reproduce, mainly because the issue depends
on NIR shaders being evicted from the shaders cache. It took a lot of
back and forth to figure out this.

Cc: mesa-stable
Signed-off-by: Samuel Pitoiset <samuel.pitoiset@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit af3b0f05fc9c7d01a9674f1046bf6389a5af47c9)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45704>
(cherry picked from commit 3159030db2d0b8297031d1595f6d736b7ebf8065)
---
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_pipeline_rt.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_pipeline_rt.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_pipeline_rt.c
index 8b50354bac5..e37b7c74f06 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_pipeline_rt.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_pipeline_rt.c
@@ -792,7 +792,12 @@ radv_rt_compile_shaders(struct radv_device *device, struct vk_pipeline_cache *ca
       if (nir_needed) {
          const bool cached = !stage->key.optimisations_disabled &&
                              !(pipeline->base.base.create_flags & VK_PIPELINE_CREATE_2_CAPTURE_DATA_BIT_KHR);
-         rt_stages[idx].stack_size = stage->nir->scratch_size;
+
+         /* On partial cache hits (when binaries are found but not NIR), the stack size is already
+          * restored from the cache but NIR must be recompiled in some cases. Do not overwrite it
+          * with the NIR scratch size which might be zero.
+          */
+         rt_stages[idx].stack_size = MAX2(rt_stages[idx].stack_size, stage->nir->scratch_size);
          rt_stages[idx].nir = radv_pipeline_cache_nir_to_handle(device, cache, stage->nir, rt_stages[idx].blake3, cached);
       }
 
